Vendored as committed source text, same shape and same rationale as
third_party/httplib and third_party/nlohmann_json — see
third_party/httplib/README.md. stb has no tagged releases, so this pins a
specific commit rather than a tag.

Re-pin by re-running:

    SHA=<new-commit>
    curl -fsSL -o third_party/stb/include/stb_image_write.h \
        "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nothings/stb/$SHA/stb_image_write.h"
    curl -fsSL -o third_party/stb/include/stb_image.h \
        "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nothings/stb/$SHA/stb_image.h"
    shasum -a 256 third_party/stb/include/stb_image_write.h third_party/stb/include/stb_image.h
    # update the two sha256 lines and the commit line above

Used by pdf-engine/writer (packing raster images into a new PDF, the
foundation for images-to-PDF / scan-to-PDF / and raster-based
merge/split/rotate/organize built on top of the existing read-only PDF
engine) and by the document-scanner image pipeline.

LOCAL PATCHES (the one deliberate deviation from the committed-verbatim
rule every other file in this directory follows):

  stb_image_write.h, stbiw__jpg_writeBits / stbiw__jpg_processDU / the
  bitBuf local in stbi_write_jpg_core: `int bitBuf` -> `unsigned int bitBuf`
  (and the pointer/parameter types that carry it). Upstream's JPEG encoder
  left-shifts this bit-packing accumulator once enough bits have
  accumulated to set its top bit, which is a left shift of a negative
  `int` — undefined behaviour in C/C++. Never observed on the macOS/Clang
  dev host; caught by UBSan inside a real Ubuntu/GCC container (same shape
  of gap this project's whole CI setup exists to catch — see the git log
  for the HKDF and conversion-engine bugs found the same way). `unsigned
  int` makes every operation on this variable well-defined modular
  arithmetic over the IDENTICAL bit pattern, so the encoded JPEG bytes are
  unchanged — this is a standards-conformance fix, not a behaviour change,
  confirmed by pdf-engine's own round-trip test (write with this encoder,
  open and render the result with the real PDFium-backed reader) passing
  before and after.

  On re-pinning to a newer commit (see "Re-pin by re-running" above): check
  whether upstream has fixed this at https://github.com/nothings/stb
  (search for stbiw__jpg_writeBits); if so, drop this patch and the
  "UAPP LOCAL PATCH" comments in the vendored file. If not, reapply it —
  grep the freshly-fetched file for "int bitBuf" to find the same three
  spots.
